  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "CRT color-incidence theorem and modulus-3p model; general power-sum criterion and quartic reductions; small-prime obstructions and integral-period partial-copy improvement; divisor-fiber transfer and finite exclusions; application of Cohen and Guralnick–Wan to all bounded degrees; generic all-slope monodromy and value-set route; explicit conic and smooth-cubic generators; concurrent independent all-conic and singular-cubic extensions; proof and manuscript review. Quantitative growing-degree full-copy estimate and clipped diagonal-fiber partial-copy theorem for affine power graphs. Degree-thirteen all-coefficient partial-copy theorem and opposite-slope certificates. Arbitrary-window image and marked-root capacity extensions and independent audit of the degree-nineteen theorem. Coupling both diagonal deletions for the stronger arbitrary-window power bound and a logarithmic degree-growth extension. Independent audit of the all-bounded-degree polynomial partial-copy theorem, its embedding-theorem reduction, finite-group constants and arithmetic-coset window argument. Uniform tuple-cover and Bonferroni route to a growing-degree arbitrary-window theorem, jointly developed with cedar_conics and independently audited.",
